  "id": "mooba_lenje",
  "name": "Mooba (Lenje spirit dance of Central Zambia)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The main dance of the Lenje of Zambia's Central Province, also practised in parts of the Copperbelt and Lusaka provinces by both men and women, at funerals, harvest, healing sessions and the installation of traditional leaders. At its peak lead dancers may be possessed by ancestral spirits called BaChooba, said to take over the flow of the dancing, drumming and singing; dancers wear rattles around the calves. It is inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage. The generic shaker card stands in for the calf rattles.",
